[
  {
    "title": "Clough Undergraduate Learning Commons",
    "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Clough%20Undergraduate%20Learning%20Commons&query_place_id=ChIJx0xM4okE9YgRG6O9OozCBy8",
    "stars": 5,
    "name": "Subhajit Bag",
    "reviewUrl": "https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m8!14m7!1m6!2m5!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pNd01GQkNSamt0VEZrNFVGWmxTbVkwV2tSdlVtYxAB!2m1!1s0x0:0x2f07c28c3abda31b!3m1!1s2@1:CAIQACodChtycF9oOjMwMFBCRjktTFk4UFZlSmY0WkRvUmc%7C0cm9V-CzMs7%7C?hl=en",
    "text": "\"The Swiss Army knife of campus buildings \ud83d\udd0b\ud83d\udcda\u2615\"\n\nThe Clough Undergraduate Learning Commons\u2014aka CULC\u2014isn\u2019t just a building. It\u2019s the campus hotspot where studying, socializing, and caffeine addiction unite in perfect harmony.\n\nWhat makes it awesome:\n\nOpen 24/7 \u2013 You can roll in at 3 a.m. to finish your lab report, cry into your notes, or discover your group project team actually can be productive.\n\nPerfect study vibes \u2013 From group pods to quiet corners, there\u2019s a spot for every flavor of academic panic.\n\nThe Starbucks downstairs \u2013 Because nothing says \u201cacademic excellence\u201d like a triple espresso at midnight.\n\nTech everywhere \u2013 Charging outlets for days, huge whiteboards, presentation rooms\u2026basically productivity paradise.\n\nLocation \u2013 Smack in the middle of campus, so you can \u201caccidentally\u201d bump into friends between classes.\n\nEvery time I walk into CULC, I feel like I\u2019m entering the mothership of Georgia Tech\u2014bright, buzzing, and brimming with brilliant people. Whether you\u2019re grinding out code, chatting over coffee, or just people-watching, this place fuels the Yellow Jacket hive mind.\n\nPro tip: The top floor is underrated\u2014great sunlight, fewer people, and a chance to feel like you\u2019re studying in a glass cloud."
  },
